296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 678 0 R
/T (1. Pad, then transform. Input is zero-padded so H/W divide cleanly by r ** len\(features\) \(so every encoder level lands on an integer size\), then x = torch.fft.fft2\(x\). From here to the end, every tensor is complex64.)
/E (1. Pad, then transform. Input is zero-padded so H/W divide cleanly by r ** len\(features\) \(so every encoder level lands on an integer size\), then x = torch.fft.fft2\(x\). From here to the end, every tensor is complex64.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
